WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.424 --> 00:00:07.006
The children walked in a slow parade toward the castle.

2
00:00:07.046 --> 00:00:09.848
They were sure that they had stepped into a fairy tale.

3
00:00:09.868 --> 00:00:35.421
At last they arrived in a large hall filled with wooden benches and Suits of armor and old

4
00:00:35.541 --> 00:00:37.183
flags stood against the walls.

5
00:00:37.203 --> 00:00:41.346
"Wait here," said the princess.

6
00:00:41.366 --> 00:00:44.008
"And don't talk while I'm gone.

7
00:00:44.329 --> 00:00:46.150
This castle is full of magic.

8
00:00:46.551 --> 00:00:48.532
I don't know what will happen if you talk."

9
00:00:49.613 --> 00:00:52.555
Jimmy wanted to say that he didn't think anything would happen.

10
00:00:53.456 --> 00:00:54.157
But he didn't.

11
00:00:55.858 --> 00:00:57.920
The princess returned, carrying a tray.

12
00:00:57.940 --> 00:01:02.524
"I could only find bread and cheese and water, but it doesn't matter.

13
00:01:02.860 --> 00:01:08.005
They'll turn into anything you like—unless you have some dreadful secret fault.

14
00:01:08.425 --> 00:01:09.566
What would you like to eat?"

15
00:01:11.748 --> 00:01:14.170
"Roast chicken," said Kathleen.

16
00:01:15.451 --> 00:01:18.874
She watched as the princess cut some bread and laid it on a plate.

17
00:01:18.894 --> 00:01:20.575
"Green peas?"

18
00:01:21.056 --> 00:01:24.338
The princess cut a piece of cheese and laid it beside the bread.

19
00:01:25.359 --> 00:01:27.261
Then she handed the plate to Kathleen.

20
00:01:28.282 --> 00:01:30.444
The boys asked for roast beef and cabbage.

21
00:01:31.776 --> 00:01:34.797
Kathleen cut the bread as if she was eating roast chicken.

22
00:01:35.818 --> 00:01:38.479
But it still looked and tasted like bread.

23
00:01:39.439 --> 00:01:43.321
She wondered what her secret fault was as she watched the boys eat their food.

24
00:01:43.341 --> 00:01:45.562
"This is a game, isn't it?"

25
00:01:46.002 --> 00:01:46.622
said Jimmy.

26
00:01:46.642 --> 00:01:49.783
"Pretending we're eating roast beef."

27
00:01:49.803 --> 00:01:52.765
"But it is beef.

28
00:01:53.225 --> 00:01:53.905
Look at it."

29
00:01:54.245 --> 00:01:56.546
The princess opened her eyes very wide.

30
00:01:56.566 --> 00:02:02.164
"Of course," said Jimmy weakly.

31
00:02:02.304 --> 00:02:03.485
"I was just joking."

32
00:02:03.985 --> 00:02:05.506
Everyone was very hungry.

33
00:02:06.367 --> 00:02:08.649
They ate and drank and felt much better.

34
00:02:08.669 --> 00:02:15.373
"Now if you're finished," said the princess, "I'll show you my treasures."

35
00:02:17.775 --> 00:02:20.516
They followed her down a long hall to some steps.

36
00:02:23.078 --> 00:02:26.220
Underneath the steps was a door hidden by a tapestry.

37
00:02:26.240 --> 00:02:33.157
"This door leads to my private apartments," said the princess.

38
00:02:35.799 --> 00:02:39.142
She guided them through a dark corridor until they came to a room.

39
00:02:40.783 --> 00:02:43.726
The princess went in first and threw open the shutters.

40
00:02:44.786 --> 00:02:47.269
The small domed room was filled with light.

41
00:02:48.289 --> 00:02:50.852
Its blue ceiling was painted with gold stars.

42
00:02:51.672 --> 00:02:52.933
But the room was empty.

43
00:02:52.953 --> 00:02:55.195
"Where are the treasures?"

44
00:02:55.595 --> 00:02:56.977
Kathleen asked politely.

45
00:02:56.997 --> 00:02:59.419
"Don't you see them?"

46
00:02:59.959 --> 00:03:00.760
said the princess.

47
00:03:02.020 --> 00:03:03.601
"No," said Jimmy.

48
00:03:03.621 --> 00:03:06.541
"And don't try fooling us again.

49
00:03:06.882 --> 00:03:07.902
There's nothing here."

50
00:03:07.922 --> 00:03:12.583
"Then I guess I'll have to say the charm," said the princess.

51
00:03:12.603 --> 00:03:14.904
"Close your eyes, please."

52
00:03:16.344 --> 00:03:18.645
The princess chanted some nonsense words.

53
00:03:19.605 --> 00:03:21.886
There was a creaking, rustling sound.

54
00:03:21.906 --> 00:03:24.047
"Open your eyes now."

55
00:03:25.867 --> 00:03:27.748
The children could not believe their eyes.

56
00:03:28.856 --> 00:03:33.380
Silver dishes, gold cups, and diamond crowns lined shelves around the room.

57
00:03:34.781 --> 00:03:37.944
All around were piles of necklaces, rings, and bracelets.

58
00:03:37.964 --> 00:03:39.866
"Oh my!"

59
00:03:40.446 --> 00:03:41.327
Gerald whispered.

60
00:03:41.347 --> 00:03:44.650
"Now do you believe I can do magic?"

61
00:03:45.190 --> 00:03:46.051
asked the princess.

62
00:03:47.192 --> 00:03:49.134
"Yes!" said Kathleen.

63
00:03:49.154 --> 00:03:50.935
"May we touch?"

64
00:03:50.955 --> 00:03:52.016
"Go ahead."

65
00:03:53.397 --> 00:03:56.160
The children had great fun playing with the treasures.

66
00:03:57.220 --> 00:03:58.881
Suddenly Kathleen had a thought.

67
00:03:59.762 --> 00:04:01.924
"Do your parents know you're awake?"

68
00:04:02.584 --> 00:04:06.387
"Oh uh yes," said the princess.

69
00:04:06.407 --> 00:04:09.789
"I told them when I got the bread and cheese.

70
00:04:10.109 --> 00:04:11.110
They're busy right now.

71
00:04:11.290 --> 00:04:12.691
Here, try this bracelet."

72
00:04:14.412 --> 00:04:16.174
"What's this old stuff over here?"

73
00:04:16.634 --> 00:04:17.254
asked Jimmy.

74
00:04:17.275 --> 00:04:19.816
"Those are all magic things!"

75
00:04:20.337 --> 00:04:21.197
said the princess.

76
00:04:21.217 --> 00:04:23.479
"What does this ring do?"

77
00:04:23.999 --> 00:04:24.700
asked Gerald.

78
00:04:26.056 --> 00:04:27.537
"It makes you invisible."

79
00:04:27.557 --> 00:04:30.078
"I'd like to try that," said Jimmy.

80
00:04:30.098 --> 00:04:35.761
"No, I'm the only one who can touch these things.

81
00:04:36.242 --> 00:04:39.143
If anyone else tries, they'll lose their magic.

82
00:04:39.503 --> 00:04:41.885
Close your eyes and I'll demonstrate the ring."

83
00:04:42.285 --> 00:04:43.626
The children closed their eyes.

84
00:04:43.646 --> 00:04:46.407
"Now count to fifty."

85
00:04:47.788 --> 00:04:49.028
Gerald counted aloud.

86
00:04:50.009 --> 00:04:52.850
Everyone could hear a creaking, rustling sound.

87
00:04:52.870 --> 00:04:53.651
49, 50."

88
00:04:56.605 --> 00:04:58.150
The children opened their eyes.

89
00:04:58.992 --> 00:05:02.182
The jewels had vanished, and so had the princess.
